Azure Functions

Azure Functions is a serverless compute service in Microsoft Azure that lets you run code without managing servers.

Key Points:
            You only write the code — Azure handles the infrastructure
            Runs code on-demand (trigger-based)
            Automatically scales up or down
            You pay only for execution time, not idle time
            Common Triggers:
            HTTP requests (APIs)
            Timers (scheduled jobs)
            Blob storage changes
            Queue messages
            Event Hub / Service Bus events
Use Cases:
            Build lightweight APIs
            Automate tasks (e.g. scheduled cleanups)
            Process files or data streams
            Integrate different services
            Simple Example:

A function runs whenever a file is uploaded to storage and processes that file.
